title: Backlash Against the RFB
subtitle: The Rotfrontkämpferbund's growing militancy is alarming would-be allies within the SPD and trade unions.
view-if: rfb_militancy >= 0.2 and not rfb_backlash_resolved
new-page: true
tags: event

= Backlash Against the RFB

The Rotfrontkämpferbund has grown ever more militant, its ranks swelling with arms, drilling, and a growing willingness to meet the SA and Stahlhelm blow for blow in the streets. Sympathetic Social Democratic workers and trade unionists, who had been drawn toward United Front actions, are increasingly alarmed. To them, the RFB no longer looks like proletarian self-defense, but like an army ready for a Bolshevik uprising. 

- @press_on: Let the RFB's militancy continue unchecked.
- @lower_militancy: Rein in the RFB to preserve our openings with Social Democratic workers.
- @justify_militancy: Argue that only a militant RFB can defend the working class from fascism.

@press_on
on-arrival: rfb_strength *= 0.95; spd_relation -= 5; labor_dissent += 5; rfb_backlash_resolved = 1; center_strength += 5*(1-dissent)

We judge that revolutionary readiness matters more than preserving ties to reformist trade unionists. Moderate sympathizers within the SPD's ranks recoil from the RFB's hardening posture, and some of our own Conciliators grumble at the lost opportunity for unity. The hardliners of the Zentralkomitee are strengthened all the same.

# TODO: this should make joint SPD actions (May Day, Iron Front counters) harder to trigger

@lower_militancy
on-arrival: rfb_militancy *= 0.5; rfb_backlash_resolved = 1

Bowing to pressure from trade unionists and Social Democratic sympathizers, we order the RFB to stand down its drilling and rhetoric, preserving the fragile threads of a United Front.

@justify_militancy
unavailable-subtitle: The moment is not yet ripe to make this argument.
choose-if: strife >= 5 and spd_relation >= 50
on-arrival: rfb_backlash_resolved = 1; spd_relation += 3

Pointing to the escalating street violence perpetrated by the SA and Stahlhelm, our agitators make the case that a militant RFB is the only guarantee against fascist terror. Enough Social Democratic workers are convinced to look past their unease, at least for now.